### ============================================
### JWT REST API Tests
### Server: https://localhost:8443
### Both /auth/* and /v1/auth/* paths are supported
### ============================================

### 1. Healthcheck
GET https://localhost:8443/v1/api/health
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. Register new user
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 2b. Register another user
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "geheim456"
}

### 3. Login as alice (save token)
# @name loginAlice
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Save Alice's token
@alice_token = {{loginAlice.response.body.token}}

### 4. Login as bob (save token)
# @name loginBob
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "geheim456"
}

### Save Bob's token
@bob_token = {{loginBob.response.body.token}}

### 5. Register with short password (should return 400)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "charlie",
  "password": "short"
}

### 6. Register with invalid username (should return 400)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user@name!",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 7. Login without password (should return 400)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice"
}

### 8. Login wrong password (should return 401)
POST https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "wrong_password"
}

### 9. Login with legacy path (/auth/ instead of /v1/auth/)
POST https://localhost:8443/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 10. Update password (requires token)
PUT https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/password
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "newSecret456"
}

### 11. Update username (requires token)
PUT https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/username
Authorization: Bearer {{alice_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice_updated"
}

### 12. Delete user (requires token)
DELETE https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/delete
Authorization: Bearer {{bob_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 13. Access without token (should return 401)
DELETE https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/user/delete
Content-Type: application/json

### 14. Wrong HTTP method (should return 405)
GET https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

### 15. Wrong path (should return 404)
GET https://localhost:8443/v1/auth/nonexistent
Content-Type: application/json

### ============================================
### Expected status codes:
### 200 OK - Success
### 201 Created - User registered
### 400 Bad Request - Missing/invalid fields
### 401 Unauthorized - Login failed / No token
### 405 Method Not Allowed - Wrong HTTP method
### 409 Conflict - Username already exists
### 429 Too Many Requests - Rate limit exceeded
### 503 Service Unavailable - Database down
### ============================================
